  SAMPLES: [
    {id:'s1',name:'Session 1 - Maya Chen.vtt',platform:'Zoom',text:"WEBVTT\n\n00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:09.000\nModerator: Walk me through how you'd pick a doctor.\n\n00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:30.000\nMaya Chen: Honestly I open the app and try to see who's available this week, but I can't tell from the list. There's no calendar until you click into each doctor.\n\n00:01:02.000 --> 00:01:14.000\nMaya Chen: I always check reviews first. If somebody has a rating under four I skip them, and I like when friends recommend someone.\n\n00:02:10.000 --> 00:02:30.000\nMaya Chen: I wanted to know if she's in-network. I had to leave the app and dig through my insurance portal to find out if I'm covered.\n\n00:03:44.000 --> 00:04:02.000\nMaya Chen: Then the form. It asked for my address and date of birth, then asked for the same information again on the next screen. Too many steps for a checkup.\n\n00:05:20.000 --> 00:05:38.000\nMaya Chen: At the end there was an extra fee I hadn't seen. I was surprised, the total cost was thirty dollars higher than the listing.\n\n00:07:01.000 --> 00:07:15.000\nMaya Chen: The text message reminder the day before was great. It gave me a heads up and I didn't forget.\n\n00:08:12.000 --> 00:08:25.000\nMaya Chen: I wasn't sure what to bring, so I just arrived with my ID. A list of paperwork would help me prepare.\n\n00:09:30.000 --> 00:09:48.000\nMaya Chen: Later I needed to reschedule and the only option was to call the office. I was on hold for ten minutes.\n\n00:11:02.000 --> 00:11:15.000\nMaya Chen: After the visit I lost the instructions. There's no visit summary in the app."},
    {id:'s2',name:'Session 2 - Daniel Ortiz.txt',platform:'Meet',text:"00:00:05 Moderator: Tell me about the last time you booked an appointment.\n00:00:20 Daniel Ortiz: Open slots matter most to me. I work shifts, so I need a calendar view across all providers, not one at a time.\n00:01:40 Daniel Ortiz: The insurance thing is confusing. It lists accepted plans but doesn't say what my copay would be.\n00:03:15 Daniel Ortiz: I re-enter my details every time I book for my kids. It's tedious.\n00:04:50 Daniel Ortiz: The price was a surprise at checkout. There was a booking fee that wasn't mentioned earlier.\n00:06:10 Daniel Ortiz: I got a reminder and a text message with directions, which was handy.\n00:07:45 Daniel Ortiz: To cancel I had to call the office during business hours. Why can't I cancel in the app?\n00:09:00 Daniel Ortiz: I'd like to know what to bring and if I need to arrive early to fill forms before."},
    {id:'s3',name:'Session 3 - Priya Nair.vtt',platform:'Teams',text:"WEBVTT\n\n00:00:03.000 --> 00:00:08.000\n<v Moderator>How did you choose your provider?</v>\n\n00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:20.000\n<v Priya Nair>I read the reviews, and the recommended badge made me pick her.</v>\n\n00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:30.000\n<v Priya Nair>No slots showed until I tapped each name. The availability is hidden.</v>\n\n00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:44.000\n<v Priya Nair>I couldn't tell if my insurance was covered until the confirmation screen.</v>\n\n00:04:00.000 --> 00:04:12.000\n<v Priya Nair>There are so many fields. The long form made me nearly give up.</v>\n\n00:06:00.000 --> 00:06:10.000\n<v Priya Nair>The reminder was nice. A heads up the morning of was perfect.</v>\n\n00:07:20.000 --> 00:07:34.000\n<v Priya Nair>I had to reschedule by phone. Nobody picked up so I left a voicemail.</v>\n\n00:09:10.000 --> 00:09:26.000\n<v Priya Nair>Nothing arrived after the visit. I'd want notes from the doctor and the follow-up plan in one place.</v>"},
  ],
